    <briefdescription>
<para>Injectable text-to-speech backend interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implement this interface to supply a real TTS encoder (e.g. a G.711 µ-law PCMU encoder for SIP, or an Opus encoder for WebRTC).</para>
<sect1 id="classthemis_1_1voice_1_1_i_tts_backend_1autotoc_md35_1s1"><sect2 id="classthemis_1_1voice_1_1_i_tts_backend_1autotoc_md35">
<title>Contract</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1voice_1_1_i_tts_backend_1a9d0167efed739d06bf0294092a1921cc" kindref="member">synthesize()</ref></computeroutput> must be thread-safe.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Each returned inner <computeroutput>vector&lt;uint8_t&gt;</computeroutput> represents one RTP payload frame (without RTP header); the session wrapper adds the correct RTP header.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>An empty outer vector indicates synthesis failure or unsupported text.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1voice_1_1_sip_call_session_1a1ba983d2a0436b8c6210f93bf2e2e008" kindref="member">SipCallSession::setTtsBackend()</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
